v 3
d ercotapi: Texas grid data from the ERCOT Public API, loaded into Stata
d
d ercotapi pulls wholesale prices, load, generation by fuel, resource
d outages and roughly a hundred other ERCOT published reports straight into
d Stata's memory.
d
d It handles three things that are awkward to do by hand.  ERCOT
d authenticates every request with two separate credentials, an OAuth bearer
d token and a subscription key sent as an HTTP header, and Stata cannot set
d custom headers.  Date filters are rejected unless sent as a From/To pair
d whose shape the error message never names.  Reports keep only a few weeks
d of history on the endpoint you would naturally query, and a request for
d anything older comes back empty with no error at all.
d
d Subcommands:
d     ercotapi setup                  check the install and your credentials
d     ercotapi catalog                list the reports you can query, with
d                                     how far back each one reaches
d     ercotapi describe <emil-id>     show a report's tables and fields
d     ercotapi pull <emil-id>, ...    query the live endpoint (recent dates)
d     ercotapi archive <emil-id>, ... download the posted files (older dates)
d
d CREDENTIALS: never stored in this package and never typed as a Stata
d argument.  Run  ercotapi setup, template  once and paste your three values
d into the file it creates.  The help file explains how to register with
d ERCOT and where the key comes from.
d
d NOTE ON THE PYTHON ENGINE: Stata cannot set the HTTP headers ERCOT
d requires, so the network work happens in two Python files that use the
d standard library only (no pip install, and Stata's own Python integration
d does not need configuring).  net install copies only recognised
d extensions, so those .py files are ancillary.  You do not need to fetch
d them by hand: on the first call ercotapi_findfile looks for them on the
d adopath, and if they are missing downloads them from this repository into
d sysdir PLUS/e/ercotapi/ and reuses the cached copies afterwards.  Override
d the source by setting global ercotapi_remote_base before the first call.
d To place them yourself instead, run: net get ercotapi, from(<this URL>)
d
d Requires: Stata 16.0 or newer, and Python 3.8 or newer on the machine
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: https://github.com/texas-2036/ercotapi-stata-public
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260920
d
f ercotapi.ado
f ercotapi_findfile.ado
f ercotapi_python.ado
f ercotapi_shell.ado
f ercotapi.sthlp
f _ercotapi_client.py
f _ercotapi_cli.py
